The four coding rules in this repository follow Andrej Karpathy's public notes on LLM coding mistakes:

https://x.com/karpathy/status/2015883857489522876

They also follow the structure of the MIT-licensed guidelines published at:

https://github.com/multica-ai/andrej-karpathy-skills

That upstream repository does not currently expose a LICENSE file through the GitHub license API. Treat the guidelines text there as someone else's work. This repository restates the four rules in its own words and links the source.

The decision to ask the user about an unresolved choice, instead of closing it inside the agent, follows Matt Pocock's grill-me and grilling skills:

https://github.com/mattpocock/skills

Those skills are MIT licensed, Copyright (c) 2026 Matt Pocock. This repository does not copy his skill text. grill-me interviews every open branch. The gap check here asks only the facts that would change the work.
